{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/architecture.md at exact head e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818 on request/lane-worktree-identity (pushed), one commit over main 359b211c, clean merge-tree onto current main c0108be8 (tree 62f9f958). Two contract additions, one per layer. Layer 6 gains \"The pending-decision read adds no projected field\": the cleanup advice reads a proposal's structural rests_on edge and the lifecycle of the commitment for the request an artifact was filed under, both already projected, so this layer gains no field, no statement kind, no admission rule and no fold profile advance, and the projection bytes are unchanged. What the read holds is that request lifecycle, candidate retirement, decision adoption and checkout removal stay four distinct facts, that a retired artifact is still a proposal's subject, and that staleness qualifies a status without ever settling a commitment. Layer 7 gains the read-only reverse association: what the worktree endpoint now reports, the five grades and why a source trailer is graded rather than believed, the bounds and the cache key, the four cleanup reports that read the same table, the derived checkout root and why it can only over-protect, and an explicit statement of what is not added -- no gs worktree command, no per-checkout record, no refs/gitseq/lanes ref, no branch field on any durable kind, no widening of the deletable set and no input to any admission decision.\n\nThree paragraphs of layer 7 are corrected at 1d7f3656 under the changes-requested verdict 19b37887 on 0d1c7e11, ratified 6803776f. The cache paragraph now names all three inputs the table is derived from -- durable frontier, ref inventory digest, captured checkout inventory digest -- and says why each is there: a cache keyed on less than its inputs stays wrong rather than going stale. A new paragraph states that every bound reports incomplete rather than a shorter answer that looks finished, lists all six incomplete conditions, keeps a genuinely unborn repository as a complete answer of nothing, and records that completion is decided in one place and the annotation step refuses to run on an incomplete table. And the cleanup paragraph no longer says the reports read the same table: the association and the cleanup classification are now described as two judgments over shared inputs, with separate caches keyed differently, neither reading the other's result, kept apart so an unsigned claim cannot reach a deletion decision.\n\nRewritten again at 557ef676 under the second changes-requested verdict 91c50bf9 on 643ab9c5, ratified 2d590023, which held that describing two observations as shared inputs did not deliver the assigned condition. Layer 7 now opens on one captured read answering the whole request -- the checkout listing taken once, the ref inventory read once, the remote resolved once, one three-second deadline and one 65,536-step budget, with both judgments reading and spending from that capture -- and says why: a second read answers about a different repository whenever a branch or a checkout moves in between, and two budgets each bound their own judgment while saying nothing about what the request costs. It states the consequence plainly, that the bound is on the request, so whichever judgment spends the budget spends it for the other and the other reports unknown. The next paragraph states what is not shared: the observation and the bound, never the conclusion, with the classifier reading no association or grade and the association reading no classification. The four reports are now described as over that captured read, and the cache as keyed under it.\n\nOne paragraph is added at this head under the third changes-requested verdict 5b80e91e on 557ef676, ratified ffd7ffc6: when the bound is reached the whole response is withheld, not the judgment that happened to notice, because a classification that finished before the budget ran out is still an answer derived from a read that never finished. It states what follows -- no candidate offered, every checkout unknown for both classification and grade, and the table saying why -- and the two structural facts that make it hold: the step can only turn an answer into unknown, and there is one way to obtain both answers together, so no caller reaches the pair without it. Rests on the behaviour artifacts at this head, not on the promise. Succeeds the live artifacts at this path in the merge target. The artifact at 557ef676 is the outside-target predecessor this head replaces; it is retired separately with this artifact as its successor.","body":{"branch":"request/lane-worktree-identity","commit":"e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c90d59242, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:558076e6112aabb153aeaede4bfa4290db5ebd8b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:63a812c58ad36267dcc57d6b2056ed4498543210, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6aaaa0373aa6f2038103c496934e43efadce1829, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7013fab03cff442c66c71f65bbb96bb939fc6364, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:72d831991ad9219879cf645d83873463e2e9f51f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8b0c8db2cbc78148b334ef80d7e996ee1a4cc775, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ea44f2caef59b11b5671d11084a569a7f4d1f3c7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:eef4b827fd5d381100ecea98d908cc27a79a91a9, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:efa3c45b7344def426a4d160c014766aa4867af3, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fd405a557524a6f54b477bbffc7bf1439982b1a1 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha